{"task_id": "Mbpp/90", "solution": "def len_log(words: list[str]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines the length of the longest string in a list of strings.\n\n    Args:\n        words: A list of strings.\n\n    Returns:\n        An integer representing the length of the longest string.\n        Returns 0 if the input list is empty.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If the input is not a list or contains non-string elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(words, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n    if not words:\n        return 0\n\n    max_length = 0\n    for word in words:\n        if not isinstance(word, str):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in the list must be strings.\")\n        if len(word) > max_length:\n            max_length = len(word)\n    return max_length"}
