{"task_id": "Mbpp/95", "solution": "def Find_Min_Length(list_of_lists: list[list]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the length of the smallest list in a list of lists.\n    Assumes list_of_lists is not empty and contains at least one list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        # According to the design, we assume list_of_lists is not empty.\n        # However, an empty list_of_lists has no smallest list length, so return 0.\n        return 0\n    \n    min_length = float('inf')\n    for inner_list in list_of_lists:\n        current_length = len(inner_list)\n        if current_length < min_length:\n            min_length = current_length\n            \n    return min_length"}
