{"task_id": "Mbpp/101", "solution": "class IndexOutOfBoundsException(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception raised when an index is out of bounds.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\ndef kth_element(array, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the kth element in the given array using 1-based indexing.\n    Raises IndexOutOfBoundsException if k is out of the array's 1-based bounds.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n    if not (1 <= k <= n):\n        raise IndexOutOfBoundsException(f\"Index {k} is out of bounds for array of length {n}.\")\n    \n    return array[k - 1]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def _factorial(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the factorial of a non-negative integer n.\"\"\"\n    res = 1\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        res *= i\n    return res\n\ndef _binomial_coefficient(n: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the binomial coefficient C(n, k).\n    Returns 0 if k is out of the valid range [0, n].\"\"\"\n    if k < 0 or k > n:\n        return 0\n    return _factorial(n) // (_factorial(k) * _factorial(n - k))\n\ndef eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the Eulerian number a(n, m).\n    It uses the formula A(n, m) = sum_{k=0}^{m} (-1)^k * C(n+1, k) * (m - k + 1)^n.\"\"\"\n    \n    eulerian_sum = 0\n    for k in range(m + 1):\n        term_sign = (-1)**k\n        term_binomial = _binomial_coefficient(n + 1, k)\n        term_power = (m - k + 1)**n\n        \n        eulerian_sum += term_sign * term_binomial * term_power\n        \n    return eulerian_sum"}
