{"task_id": "Mbpp/113", "solution": "def check_integer(input_string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if the given string represents a valid integer.\n    A valid integer string consists solely of digits, optionally prefixed\n    by a single '+' or '-' sign.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_string:\n        return False\n\n    s = input_string\n    if s[0] == '+' or s[0] == '-':\n        s = s[1:]\n\n    return s.isdigit() and bool(s)"}
