{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def odd_Equivalent(binary_string: str, num_rotations: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the number of unique decimal values that are odd when rotating a binary string.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _rotate_string(s: str, k: int) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Rotates a string s by k positions to the left.\"\"\"\n        k = k % len(s)\n        return s[k:] + s[:k]\n\n    def _binary_to_decimal(binary_str: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Converts a binary string to its decimal integer value.\"\"\"\n        return int(binary_str, 2)\n\n    def _is_odd(decimal_val: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a decimal integer value is odd.\"\"\"\n        return decimal_val % 2 != 0\n\n    unique_rotations_set = set()\n    odd_count = 0\n    current_binary_string = binary_string\n    n = len(binary_string)\n\n    # We only need to rotate up to n times, as rotations repeat after that.\n    # The actual number of rotations considered is min(num_rotations, n).\n    # Since we are adding to a set, unique rotations are handled.\n    for _ in range(min(num_rotations, n)):\n        if current_binary_string not in unique_rotations_set:\n            unique_rotations_set.add(current_binary_string)\n            decimal_value = _binary_to_decimal(current_binary_string)\n            if _is_odd(decimal_value):\n                odd_count += 1\n        current_binary_string = _rotate_string(current_binary_string, 1)\n        \n    return odd_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "def common_in_nested_lists(list_of_lists: list[list]) -> set:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds elements common to all sub-lists within a given nested list.\n    Returns a set of these common elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        return set()\n\n    # Initialize common_elements with the set of the first sub-list.\n    # If the first sub-list is empty, common_elements will be an empty set.\n    common_elements = set(list_of_lists[0])\n\n    # Iterate through the remaining sub-lists and intersect with common_elements.\n    for sublist in list_of_lists[1:]:\n        common_elements.intersection_update(sublist)\n        # Optimization: if common_elements becomes empty, no more common elements can be found.\n        if not common_elements:\n            break\n\n    return common_elements"}
