{"task_id": "Mbpp/116", "solution": "def tuple_to_int(input_tuple: tuple) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a tuple of positive integers into a single integer.\n    It validates input type and elements, raising errors for invalid inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_tuple, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a tuple.\")\n\n    string_representations = []\n    for element in input_tuple:\n        if not isinstance(element, int) or element <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"All elements in the tuple must be positive integers.\")\n        string_representations.append(str(element))\n\n    combined_string = \"\".join(string_representations)\n    return int(combined_string)"}
