{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def max_sum(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence in the given array.\n    A bitonic subsequence is first increasing and then decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return arr[0]\n\n    # _calculate_lis_sum_ending_at_i(arr)\n    lis_sums = [0] * n\n    for i in range(n):\n        lis_sums[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i]:\n                lis_sums[i] = max(lis_sums[i], lis_sums[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # _calculate_lds_sum_starting_at_i(arr)\n    lds_sums = [0] * n\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        lds_sums[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i]:\n                lds_sums[i] = max(lds_sums[i], lds_sums[j] + arr[i])\n    \n    max_bitonic_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        # Subtract arr[i] because it's included in both LIS and LDS sums\n        current_bitonic_sum = lis_sums[i] + lds_sums[i] - arr[i]\n        max_bitonic_sum = max(max_bitonic_sum, current_bitonic_sum)\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "import math\n\ndef next_Perfect_Square(input_number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates and returns the smallest perfect square strictly greater than the input integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if input_number < 0:\n        return 0\n\n    root = math.isqrt(input_number)\n\n    if root * root == input_number:\n        next_root = root + 1\n    else:\n        next_root = root + 1\n\n    return next_root * next_root"}
