{"task_id": "Mbpp/305", "solution": "def start_withp(word_list: list[str]) -> tuple[str, str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the first two words from a list of strings that start with 'p' or 'P'.\n    \"\"\"\n    found_p_words = []\n\n    def _is_p_starting(word: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Helper to check if a word starts with 'p' or 'P' case-insensitively.\"\"\"\n        return word.lower().startswith('p')\n\n    for s in word_list:\n        words_in_string = s.split()\n        for word in words_in_string:\n            if _is_p_starting(word):\n                found_p_words.append(word)\n                if len(found_p_words) == 2:\n                    return (found_p_words[0], found_p_words[1])\n    return ('', '') # Should not be reached based on the assert, but good practice."}
