{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "def max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr: list[int], n: int, i: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence.\n    The subsequence must include elements from arr[0...i] (prefix)\n    and must include arr[k] (where k > i).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not (0 <= i < n and 0 <= k < n and k > i):\n        # This case should ideally be handled by input validation outside,\n        # but for robustness based on problem context.\n        # If i or k are out of bounds, or k is not greater than i,\n        # it might imply an invalid scenario.\n        # Assuming valid inputs as per prompt \"No isinstance() checks or raise exceptions\"\n        pass\n\n    # dp[p] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence\n    # ending at index p, where all elements in the subsequence are < arr[k].\n    dp = [0] * (i + 1)\n    max_prefix_sum = 0\n\n    for p in range(i + 1):\n        if arr[p] < arr[k]:\n            dp[p] = arr[p]\n            for prev in range(p):\n                if arr[p] > arr[prev] and arr[prev] < arr[k]:\n                    dp[p] = max(dp[p], dp[prev] + arr[p])\n            max_prefix_sum = max(max_prefix_sum, dp[p])\n\n    return max_prefix_sum + arr[k]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "def set_left_most_unset_bit(input_integer: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets the leftmost unset bit in the given integer.\n\n    Args:\n        input_integer: The integer to manipulate.\n\n    Returns:\n        The integer with its leftmost unset bit set.\n    \"\"\"\n    if input_integer == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Find the position of the most significant bit + 1.\n    # This acts as an upper bound for our search or the position\n    # if all bits up to the current MSB are set.\n    search_limit = input_integer.bit_length()\n\n    # Initialize the position of the leftmost unset bit.\n    # By default, assume it's one position to the left of the current MSB\n    # (i.e., if all lower bits are set).\n    unset_bit_position = search_limit\n\n    # Iterate from the bit just to the left of the MSB down to 0\n    # to find the leftmost unset bit.\n    for pos in range(search_limit - 1, -1, -1):\n        # Check if the bit at 'pos' is unset (0)\n        if not (input_integer >> pos) & 1:\n            unset_bit_position = pos\n            break # Found the leftmost unset bit\n\n    # Set the identified bit using a bitwise OR operation.\n    return input_integer | (1 << unset_bit_position)"}
