{"task_id": "Mbpp/409", "solution": "def min_product_tuple(input_list: list[tuple[int | float, int | float]]) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum product from pairs of tuples within a given list.\n    The function performs input validation before calculating products and finding the minimum.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_list, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n    if not input_list:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list cannot be empty.\")\n\n    min_product = float('inf')\n    for item in input_list:\n        if not isinstance(item, tuple):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in the input list must be tuples.\")\n        if len(item) != 2:\n            raise ValueError(\"Each tuple must contain exactly two numerical elements.\")\n        \n        element1, element2 = item\n        if not isinstance(element1, (int, float)) or not isinstance(element2, (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(\"Tuple elements must be numerical (int or float).\")\n\n        product = element1 * element2\n        if product < min_product:\n            min_product = product\n            \n    return min_product"}
