{"task_id": "Mbpp/437", "solution": "class String:\n    \"\"\"\n    Encapsulates a string value and provides core logic for character removal.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, input_string: str):\n        self._value = input_string\n\n    def removeEvenIndexedCharacters(self) -> 'String':\n        \"\"\"\n        Returns a new String object with characters from odd 0-based indices.\n        \"\"\"\n        result_chars = []\n        for i, char in enumerate(self._value):\n            if i % 2 != 0:  # Retain characters at odd indices\n                result_chars.append(char)\n        return String(\"\".join(result_chars))\n\n    def get_value(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"\n        Retrieves the encapsulated string value.\n        \"\"\"\n        return self._value\n\ndef remove_odd(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes characters at even 0-based indices from an input string, leveraging the String class.\n    \"\"\"\n    string_obj = String(input_string)\n    processed_string_obj = string_obj.removeEvenIndexedCharacters()\n    return processed_string_obj.get_value()"}
