{"task_id": "Mbpp/473", "solution": "class _NormalizedTuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Encapsulates a tuple's elements in a sorted, hashable form for order-independent comparison.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, original_tuple: tuple):\n        self._elements = tuple(sorted(original_tuple))\n\n    def __eq__(self, other) -> bool:\n        if not isinstance(other, _NormalizedTuple):\n            return NotImplemented\n        return self._elements == other._elements\n\n    def __hash__(self) -> int:\n        return hash(self._elements)\n\n    def __repr__(self) -> str:\n        return f\"_NormalizedTuple({self._elements})\"\n\n    def to_original_form(self) -> tuple:\n        \"\"\"Returns the normalized tuple in its sorted form.\"\"\"\n        return self._elements\n\ndef tuple_intersection(list1: list[tuple], list2: list[tuple]) -> set[tuple]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the intersection of two lists of tuples, treating tuples as equivalent\n    irrespective of element order.\n    \"\"\"\n    normalized_set1 = set()\n    for original_tuple in list1:\n        normalized_set1.add(_NormalizedTuple(original_tuple))\n\n    normalized_set2 = set()\n    for original_tuple in list2:\n        normalized_set2.add(_NormalizedTuple(original_tuple))\n\n    intersection_normalized = normalized_set1.intersection(normalized_set2)\n\n    result_set = set()\n    for normalized_tuple_obj in intersection_normalized:\n        result_set.add(normalized_tuple_obj.to_original_form())\n\n    return result_set"}
