{"task_id": "Mbpp/476", "solution": "def big_sum(arr: list) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sum of the largest and smallest value in a given array.\n    This function uses built-in min() and max() for efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0  # Or handle as an error based on broader context, but for sum of min/max, 0 is a neutral return for an empty list.\n                  # The requirement does not ask for error handling, so returning 0 for empty list is a safe assumption.\n    \n    smallest_val = min(arr)\n    largest_val = max(arr)\n    return smallest_val + largest_val"}
