{"task_id": "Mbpp/556", "solution": "def find_Odd_Pair(input_list: list[int], length: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of pairs in the input list whose XOR sum is odd.\n    An XOR sum is odd if and only if one number is odd and the other is even.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_pair_count = 0\n    for i in range(length):\n        for j in range(i + 1, length):\n            num1 = input_list[i]\n            num2 = input_list[j]\n\n            is_num1_odd = (num1 % 2 != 0)\n            is_num2_odd = (num2 % 2 != 0)\n\n            if is_num1_odd != is_num2_odd:\n                odd_pair_count += 1\n\n    return odd_pair_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/558", "solution": "def digit_distance_nums(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of per-digit absolute differences between two integers.\n\n    The shorter integer is implicitly padded with leading zeros to match the length\n    of the longer integer for digit comparison.\n    \"\"\"\n    str_num1 = str(num1)\n    str_num2 = str(num2)\n\n    max_len = max(len(str_num1), len(str_num2))\n\n    padded_str_num1 = str_num1.zfill(max_len)\n    padded_str_num2 = str_num2.zfill(max_len)\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(max_len):\n        digit1 = int(padded_str_num1[i])\n        digit2 = int(padded_str_num2[i])\n        total_sum += abs(digit1 - digit2)\n\n    return total_sum"}
