{"task_id": "Mbpp/577", "solution": "def last_Digit_Factorial(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the last digit of the factorial of a given non-negative integer n.\n    Handles special cases for 0!, 1!, and n! for n >= 5.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0 or n == 1:\n        return 1\n    elif n >= 5:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 6\n    elif n == 4:\n        return 4\n    # The problem implies n is non-negative, and all cases 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, and >=5 are covered.\n    # No other cases are possible for valid non-negative integer input."}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/576", "solution": "def is_Sub_Array(list1: list, list2: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if list2 is a sublist of list1.\n    A sublist is defined as a contiguous sequence of elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list2:\n        return True\n    if not list1 and list2:\n        return False\n\n    n = len(list1)\n    m = len(list2)\n\n    if m > n:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(n - m + 1):\n        if list1[i:i+m] == list2:\n            return True\n    return False"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/573", "solution": "from typing import List, Union\n\ndef unique_product(input_list: List[Union[int, float]]) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the product of unique numbers in a given list.\n\n    The product is 1 if the list of unique numbers is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    unique_numbers = set(input_list)\n    product = 1\n    for num in unique_numbers:\n        product *= num\n    return product"}
