{"task_id": "Mbpp/630", "solution": "def get_coordinates(coordinate: tuple[int, int]) -> list[list[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates all 3x3 adjacent coordinates for a given input coordinate, including itself,\n    and returns them sorted by x-component then by y-component.\n    \"\"\"\n    x, y = coordinate\n    adjacent_coords = []\n    for dx in range(-1, 2):\n        for dy in range(-1, 2):\n            adjacent_coords.append([x + dx, y + dy])\n    \n    # The current iteration order naturally sorts by x then y, so explicit sort is redundant but harmless.\n    # It sorts by dx, then dy, which translates to sorting by x, then y.\n    # For example, for (3,4):\n    # dx=-1: [2,3], [2,4], [2,5]\n    # dx=0:  [3,3], [3,4], [3,5]\n    # dx=1:  [4,3], [4,4], [4,5]\n    # This matches the desired output order.\n    return adjacent_coords"}
