{"task_id": "Mbpp/754", "solution": "def extract_index_list(l1: list, l2: list, l3: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Finds elements common to three lists at the same index.\n\n    Args:\n        l1: The first input list.\n        l2: The second input list.\n        l3: The third input list.\n\n    Returns:\n        A list containing elements that are common across l1, l2, and l3\n        at the same index.\n    \"\"\"\n    common_elements = []\n    min_length = min(len(l1), len(l2), len(l3))\n    for i in range(min_length):\n        if l1[i] == l2[i] == l3[i]:\n            common_elements.append(l1[i])\n    return common_elements"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/752", "solution": "def jacobsthal_num(n: int) -> int:\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 1\n    else:\n        # Calculate iteratively to find the nth Jacobsthal number.\n        # Uses the recurrence J_n = J_(n-1) + 2 * J_(n-2).\n        a, b = 0, 1 # Corresponds to J_0 and J_1\n        for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n            a, b = b, a + 2 * b\n        return a"}
