{"task_id": "Mbpp/757", "solution": "def _reverse_string(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Reverses a given string.\"\"\"\n    return s[::-1]\n\ndef count_reverse_pairs(string_list: list[str]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts unique reverse string pairs in the given list.\"\"\"\n    pair_count = 0\n    processed_strings = set()\n    \n    # Convert list to a set for efficient lookup of reversed strings.\n    original_string_set = set(string_list)\n\n    for s1 in string_list:\n        if s1 not in processed_strings:\n            s2 = _reverse_string(s1)\n            \n            # Check if s1 is not its own reverse, s2 exists in the original list, and s2 hasn't been processed.\n            if s1 != s2 and s2 in original_string_set and s2 not in processed_strings:\n                pair_count += 1\n                processed_strings.add(s1)\n                processed_strings.add(s2)\n                \n    return pair_count"}
